From: OpenAI RV220W promotion toolkit <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] staging: octeon: accept DSA conduit length-mismatch frames

The Octeon PIP parser reports receive error 10 when the frame length does
not agree with the value occupying the normal Ethernet length/type field.
EtherType-inserting DSA tags, including the Broadcom tag used by B53,
occupy that location until the DSA receive path removes the tag.  As a
result, otherwise valid tagged frames can be dropped by the Octeon driver
before eth_type_trans() hands them to DSA.

Keep the existing short-frame exception and also accept error 10 on a
netdev which is actively used as a DSA conduit.  The normal DSA receive
path remains responsible for validating and decoding the tag; unrelated
Octeon ports retain the existing error handling.

This is a generic Octeon/DSA conduit compatibility fix.  It does not add
B53-, board-name-, or OpenWrt-specific behavior.

--- a/drivers/staging/octeon/ethernet-rx.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/octeon/ethernet-rx.c
@@ -18,5 +18,6 @@
 #include <linux/smp.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
+#include <net/dsa.h>
 #include <net/dst.h>
 #ifdef CONFIG_XFRM
 #include <linux/xfrm.h>
@@ -69,7 +70,11 @@ static inline int cvm_oct_check_rcv_error(struct cvmx_wqe *work)
 	else
 		port = work->word1.cn38xx.ipprt;
 
-	if ((work->word2.snoip.err_code == 10) && (work->word1.len <= 64))
+	if (work->word2.snoip.err_code == 10 &&
+	    (work->word1.len <= 64 ||
+	     (port < TOTAL_NUMBER_OF_PORTS &&
+	      cvm_oct_device[port] &&
+	      netdev_uses_dsa(cvm_oct_device[port]))))
 		/*
 		 * Ignore length errors on min size packets. Some
 		 * equipment incorrectly pads packets to 64+4FCS
